        "title": "stm32: harden use of RNG functions",
        "user": {
            "login": "dpgeorge",
            "id": 6187689,
            "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjYxODc2ODk=",
            "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6187689?v=4",
            "gravatar_id": "",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/users/dpgeorge",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/dpgeorge",
            "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/dpgeorge/followers",
            "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/dpgeorge/following{/other_user}",
            "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/dpgeorge/gists{/gist_id}",
            "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/dpgeorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
            "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/dpgeorge/subscriptions",
            "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/dpgeorge/orgs",
            "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/dpgeorge/repos",
            "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/dpgeorge/events{/privacy}",
            "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/dpgeorge/received_events",
            "type": "User",
            "user_view_type": "public",
            "site_admin": false
        },
        "body": "### Summary\r\n\r\nFour commits to harden the use of random functions in the stm32 port:\r\n- `stm32/boards/NUCLEO_H723ZG`: Enable `MICROPY_HW_ENABLE_RNG`, instead of using fall-back PRNG code.\r\n- `stm32/mpconfigport`: Only enable `RANDOM_SEED_INIT_FUNC` if hardware RNG is available.\r\n- `stm32/mphalport`: Only build `mp_hal_get_random()` if hardware RNG is available.\r\n- `stm32/rng`: Remove PRNG implementation of `rng_get()`, as it's no longer needed.\r\n\r\nSee related discussion #19588\r\n\r\n### Testing\r\n\r\nBuild affected boards to make sure they still link.\r\n\r\nTODO: test on NUCLEO_H723ZG.\r\n\r\n### Trade-offs and Alternatives\r\n\r\nThis removes the PRNG version of `rng_get()`.  Could instead leave that code in and rename the function to `prng_get()` to make it more obvious what the implementation is.  But it's not really needed and best to avoid future mistakes using it in the wrong way.\r\n\r\n### Generative AI\r\n\r\nI did not use generative AI tools when creating this PR.\r\n",
